  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_020: scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.715 accuracy, and the largest single gain came from upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L. However, all multiprofile experiments so far have used concat fusion exclusively, leaving the fusion strategy as an untested design lever in the best-performing regime. Config_027 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted relative to config_020, providing a clean single-variable comparison. This is the most informative next step because: (1) it directly tests whether learned modality weighting can further improve on the current best, (2) it isolates the fusion effect without confounding changes to encoder, aggregation, or profile setting, and (3) the result will clarify whether further gains should be sought in fusion, RNA encoder (e.g., scgpt), or aggregation (e.g., transformer) under the ViT-L setting, guiding subsequent experiments efficiently under the limited budget."
}

